    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Attractive detached 3 / 4 -Bed home on c 0.7 acres in a tranquil setting. Close to numerous beaches, attractions and amenities.\t\r\nOffers in excess of €400,000\r\n\r\n‘Gaoth na Mara’ is an attractive 3 / 4 -Bedroom detached dormer-style residence set in a peaceful cul-de-sac of just three homes. Built c. 2005 and extending to approximately 130 sqm. the property offers bright, well-balanced accommodation with generous living spaces, a sun lounge, three bedrooms and excellent outdoor space on approximately 0.7 acres of mature private grounds. The home enjoys a tranquil rural setting while remaining within easy reach of Duncannon, Fethard-on-Sea and the beautiful beaches, villages and attractions of the Hook Peninsula. Presented in good order throughout, this inviting home with attractive stone cut exterior, combines character finishes with practical everyday living. The dual-aspect living room opens through double doors to a bright triple-aspect sun lounge, while the kitchen/dining room provides a welcoming country-style heart to the home. Outside, the private lawned grounds, mature tree boundaries and ample off-street parking create an appealing setting for families, holidaymakers or those seeking a quieter coastal retreat.\r\n\r\nThe location is a major feature: Duncannon Beach, local pubs and restaurants are only minutes away, with Fethard-on-Sea offering everyday amenities including shops, supermarket, pharmacy and hospitality options. The wider Hook Peninsula is renowned for sandy beaches, secluded coves, coastal scenery, historic attractions and leisure pursuits, including Hook Lighthouse, Duncannon Fort, Baginbun, Dollar Bay, Booley Bay and other well-known coastal destinations. New Ross, Wexford Town and Waterford City are all accessible for wider services and commuting.\r\nIDEAL FAMILY HOME OR HOLIDAY GET-AWAY!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Greeting Hall\t    1.97m x 1.15m tiled flooring, PVC entrance door with sidelights, \r\nInner Hall            3.43m x 2.99m wood panelled ceiling, feature hand-crafted wooden staircase to upper floor and shelved hot-press.\r\nLiving Room\t    5.97m x 3.46 dual aspect room with semi-solid Oak flooring, wood panelled ceiling, feature metal fireplace with wood mantel and slate hearth, TV point and double wooden door to sun lounge.\r\nSun Lounge\t    3.98m x 2.96m with semi-solid Oak flooring, bright triple aspect room with vaulted wood panelled ceiling with recessed lighting and door access to rear garden area.\r\nKitchen/ Dining    5.97m x 3.48m dual aspect room with tile flooring and wood panelled ceiling, country kitchen with laminate counter tops and tile splash back, stainless sink, Belling free standing 5-ring gas hob with electric oven, extractor fan and tile splash back, dishwasher and access to utility.\r\nUtility Room         1.89m x 0.97m tile flooring, laminate countertop, washing machine hook-up and back door access to rear garden.\r\nGuest WC            2.39m x 1.88m tile flooring, wainscoting, full bathtub with tile surround and overhead shower, WHB and WC.\r\nGallery Landing   3.96m x 2.97m solid wood flooring, vaulted ceiling with skylight and access to attic. \r\nBedroom 1           3.47m x 2.89m solid wood flooring and dormer window to front.\r\nBedroom 2           3.47m x 2.89m solid wood flooring, dormer window overlooking large rear lawn area, \r\nBedroom 3           5.98m x 3.48m large dual aspect room (formerly 2 bedrooms!) with solid wood flooring, dormer windows overlooking front and large rear lawn area, en-suite.\r\nEn-Suite              1.86m x 1.79m tile flooring, wainscoting, vaulted ceiling with skylight, enclosed shower unit, WC and WHB.\r\nWC                      1.87m x 1.08m tile flooring, vaulted ceiling with skylight, WC, WHB"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Attractive 3 / 4 -Bed detached dormer-style residence extending to c 130 sqm.\r\nSet on c. 0.7 acres of private mature lawned grounds with ample off-street parking.\r\nBright dual and triple-aspect living spaces.\r\nTranquil location with beautiful countryside views.\r\nClose to numerous beaches and coastline of the Hook Peninsula with famous lighthouse. \r\nMinutes to Duncannon and bustling Fethard-on-Sea, with amenities, pubs, restaurants etc. \r\nLess than 30 minutes to New Ross town, 30 minutes to Waterford City via ferry."
      },
